# Local development: serve from Caddy's internal CA instead of a public one.
#
# Point TLS_DIR at this directory (see "Running it locally" in README.md) when
# running the stack on a machine the production domain does not resolve to.
# Caddy then issues a locally-trusted-looking certificate and never contacts
# Let's Encrypt — so a local run cannot burn the domain's ACME rate limits
# (5 failed validations per hour, and a week-long lockout after repeats).
#
# Browsers will warn until you trust Caddy's local root, which is the point:
# the certificate is for this machine only, never for a real deployment.
tls internal
